Package: voltaic
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: jcfs <jcfs@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, python3-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-3.0
Recommends: gir1.2-xapp-1.0
Suggests: gir1.2-ayatanaappindicator3-0.1
Homepage: https://github.com/jcfs/voltaic
Description: Wireless device battery levels in the system tray
 Voltaic shows the charge of Logitech keyboards and mice, and of AirPods
 down to each earbud and the case, in a translucent tray panel. Hover the
 icon for a gauge per device; click to keep it open.
 .
 It speaks Logitech's HID++ over /dev/hidraw and Apple's accessory protocol
 over an L2CAP socket directly, using only the Python standard library.
 Solaar is not required, and neither is root.
 .
 This package installs the udev rules that grant the logged-in user access
 to the Logitech hidraw nodes, so no manual setup is needed.
